# armillary — deny by default.
#
# The router's working directory PHYSICALLY CONTAINS every module composed into it —
# each an independent git repo, none a submodule. So this file's job is not build
# artifacts: it keeps the router from swallowing its guests, and keeps a studio's
# private composition out of a public repo.
#
# The model is an ALLOWLIST. Everything in the root is ignored, and the lines below
# re-include exactly what the router IS — the set `modules.toml` declares in
# [router] contains. A guest is ignored because it was never allowed, not because
# someone remembered to name it. Forgetting is therefore safe, and no studio-specific
# directory name ever has to appear in this public file.
#
# Adding a newly tracked file to the router means adding an allow line here. That
# friction is deliberate: this repo publishes, so publication should be a choice.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/getting-started.md
!/philosophy.md
!/self.md
!/modules.toml

# ── composition slots ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The slot directories ship their READMEs and nothing else; whatever is composed
# into them is the user's own independent git repo. The router never tracks its
# guests — that is what "operator-agnostic" means on disk. (A slot must be
# re-included before its contents can be re-excluded: git will not descend into
# an ignored directory.)

!/operators/
/operators/*
!/operators/README.md

!/repos/
/repos/*
!/repos/README.md

# ── what the allowlist already covers, listed only so it is legible ──────────
# None of these needs a rule; `/*` has them. Recorded so a reader can see that
# the coverage is intentional rather than accidental:
#
#   the commons — at `commons/` or at whatever name a workspace gives it
#   modules.local.toml, CLAUDE.local.md — the private overlay. Usually symlinks
#     into the commons, where the canonical files are synced and version-controlled.
#   models -> operators — the 2026-07-24 rename compat symlink
#   .claude/ .pi/ .superpowers/ .obsidian/ — per-machine harness and editor state
#   system/, local/ — machine-local working directories

**/.DS_Store
